WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.620
This girl is Kouyama Mitsuki, 12 years old.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.920
Since <i>"Myself"</i>  is a big hit, she asked Dr. Wakaouji to listen to it...

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.760
...but he said that he didn't listen to music.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.860
We tried very hard to make him listen...

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.230
...and somehow, we ended up at the grave site of Mitsuki's parents.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.040
It was there that we found about his true feelings towards music.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.910
It looks like that girl was moved by them.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.070
Well, then...{Missing line}

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.870
...I wonder what's going to happen today.{Missing line}

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.500
Huh?{Missing line}

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.820
Do you understand?{Missing line}

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.760
Yes.{Missing line}

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.410
Ah, found her!

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.220
This is her!

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:10.810
Eh?

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.240
Who is it?

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.230
I'll be on TV with her tomorrow.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.000
Komaki Fuyuko, is she a geisha?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.380
Stupid, not everyone who wears
 a kimono is a geisha.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.700
She's an Enka singer.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.200
An Enka singer?

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.880
Why do you have to appear with her? {Oh yeah! Mitsuki is okay to appear with a geisha instead. Meroko no Baaaka}

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.970
You <i>are</i>  an idol, aren't you?

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.200
I think it's because...

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.670
...Komaki-san has been hosting a show for new idols lately. {I feel like something's untranslated here, I will beep convex to confirm}

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.110
So, I'll be a guest on her show.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.590
What's this?

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.780
"Do you want the next generation to live by strict rules?"

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.180
Looks like new idols have to go through this gateway for success.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.980
"Gateway for success?"

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.220
What's that?

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.230
It means something like 
the road to stardom.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.710
You should have said so from the start.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.190
"Gateway for success...", he said.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.770
Old man Takuto... gross!

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:11.070
Haha, Meroko, you didn't 
even know what it meant. {the and was unneeded}

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.410
T-That's not true!

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.370
Besides, I'm older than you, Takuto!

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:21.130
Well, if I'm an old man, that makes Meroko an old hag, right?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.840
What?!

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.050
Now you've done it! {Takuto no Baka! He transformed to get some spanking :D}

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.040
What was that?

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:26.760
Stop it!

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:31.000
I'm only a little bit older than you!

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.920
Wow, the TV station is so big!

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.250
I guess so.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.630
Ah, my favorite weather woman!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.560
Wah, so she's here too...

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.050
Ah, that guy... I saw him in a magazine!

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:11.360
Aww, If only I had some 
papers for autographs...

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.550
Stop it, Mitsuki.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:13.970
Eh?

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.380
You're already one of them.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.940
Uh, s-sorry.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.570
By the way, when we meet Komaki-san, make sure to greet her properly.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.240
Komaki-san is really annoyed by small details.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.000
Okay.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.120
The proper greeting in showbiz is not "Good afternoon!", but {Japanese showbiz etiquette is weird}

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.620
Good morning!

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.370
Good morning!

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.200
Good morning!

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:37.870
Good morning!

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:38.830
Good morning!

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.360
Nice to meet you today.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.420
Good morning!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.570
Ah, trouble!

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.140
Good morning, Komaki-san!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.880
I'm the manager for your 
guest <i>Full Moon</i>  today.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.310
My name's Ooshige.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:58.970
Pleasure.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.640
And <i>Full Moon</i>-san is.. where?{}

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:01.990
Eh?

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:10.900
Let's go, Tadokoro.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.640
Erm, um...

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.410
Well, we'll see you later.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.380
G-Good day! {Oh no}

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.960
Hey, wasn't that Komaki just now?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.060
Eh? That was Komaki-san?

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:43.560
That's right!

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:44.730
I'm a failure.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.560
Why didn't you come with me?

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.350
Eh?

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.220
You didn't know that was Komaki-san?

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:52.760
I'm sorry.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.260
She wasn't wearing a kimono, so...

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:56.820
Enka singers wear jeans, too.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.490
So, did you greet her properly?

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.460
Eh... sort of...

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.740
I'm kind of worried.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:09.270
Listen!

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.890
This time, say "Good Morning!" 
when you greet her.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.370
Okay!

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.150
Here we go.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:20.060
Excuse me, this is Ooshige.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.280
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.990
Once more, seriously this time. {Edit block}

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.520
This is <i>Full Moon</i>, 
and I'm her manager Ooshige.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.180
Good morning!

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:31.620
I'm <i>Full Moon</i>.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.990
I'm looking forward to working with you today.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.560
How do you do? I'm Komaki.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:37.700
I'm also looking forward to today.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:42.420
She's still new, so I think she could have some problems...

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.890
Ah, how wonderful!

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.670
W-Wait, Mitsuki-chan!

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.170
Wow, the kimono is so pretty.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.880
Komaki-san, it looks like 
you're going to Shichigosan.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.000
I really messed up...

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.940
And Ooshige-san doesn't 
look too happy either...

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.020
What should I do?

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.240
It's all my fault.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:17.720
Aside from that, that Komaki's a mean old hag.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.490
Shut it.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:25.440
Man, that Komaki's a mean old hag, right?{}

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:26.300
Huh?

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.210
And that bald manager is 
such a stick-in-the-mud.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.920
Tadokoro, is it?

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.130
He sure is one.{}

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.550
He's such an ass kisser.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:38.120
Weren't you doing that to Komaki as well?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.640
Well, you have no choice in order to advance your career in showbiz.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:41.760
There's no helping that.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.850
Rehearsal is starting, we should get going.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:47.990
Okay, okay.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:50.920
What was that about?

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.310
It's so disgusting.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:54.240
Should you be saying that?

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.610
She should have put it out properly.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.490
You! {It's not what it looks like, honest}

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.510
What are you doing with that cigarette?

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.070
You're still a teenager!

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:02.900
Eh?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.800
Really... all the new talents these days...

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:07.620
Ah, you're mistaken.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.430
The girl who just left 
didn't put it out properly.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:11.290
That's why I...

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.250
How dare you talk back...!

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:15.750
Man, kids these days...

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:17.630
In the old days, you wouldn't even think about doing that.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:18.470
Eh?

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.800
Um...

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.860
That's not how it was...

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.960
She really is a mean old hag!

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.440
This girl would never smoke!

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.850
Ah, she's really pissing me off!

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:35.840
Hey, Meroko!

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.630
Where do you think you're going?

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.360
Eh... wait, you two!

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:40.160
Mitsuki!

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.780
Rehearsal is starting soon.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:46.740
Do your best so Komaki-san 
won't get mad at you. {Too late}

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:48.230
Yes.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:51.850
Test! Test!

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.670
A! A! A!

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:56.040
Mic check!

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.390
Mic check!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.400
Whoa!{}

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.010
Check, one, two!

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.090
Check, one, two!

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.390
There's so many staff members here.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:08.290
That's right.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.990
They're working hard 
to broadcast your song.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:15.560
Well, <i>Full Moon</i>-san, we're on standby, so please go on.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:16.950
See, now, good luck.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:17.820
R-Right!

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.330
Okay, let's try it.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.320
Well, we'll start in...

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.160
Five seconds...

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:30.910
Four.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:31.890
Three.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:48.520
Cut!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.600
What is she doing?

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:52.160
Are you okay?

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:52.990
I'm sorry.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.980
The camera appeared so suddenly... 
I was surprised.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:56.330
Ah, I see.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:59.190
We're doing the same thing this time, so please don't be startled by it, okay?

00:09:59.190 --> 00:09:59.920
Okay.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:01.480
Alright, let's try again!

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:06.730
Five seconds...

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:07.350
Four.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:08.320
Three.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.210
After the intro, start the lasers...

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:23.050
Ready and go!

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:35.980
Whoa, whoa! {Deadly lazors}

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.270
Cut!

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:42.530
Does she think something will happen if the lasers touch her?

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:46.340
Let's clean up and start with Komaki-san.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:46.720
Okay.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.280
Alright then, let's get moving!

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:54.750
Excuse me, you can take a short break now, so if you could tell <i>Full Moon</i>-san...

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:55.760
Alright.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.960
I'll try to calm her down.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.710
Well, please do.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.120
Take a break!

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:22.830
Well?

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:27.070
What exactly is your reason to fly out here, leaving her all alone?

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:29.700
There's the one. {edited}

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:30.380
Eh?

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:33.080
There! That guy!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:33.700
Huh?

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:37.710
From that magazine she was reading last night... one of the band members!

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.000
He's so cool!

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.360
Hello?!

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.470
Weren't you looking for Komaki?!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.200
Geez, you're so annoying.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.930
A little distraction won't hurt.

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:55.640
Could it be...

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:58.180
Maybe you're jealous?

00:11:58.180 --> 00:11:59.020
Huh?

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.260
Why should I be jealous?

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:06.000
Maybe because this is the date
 that I've longed for?

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.560
Well, it's too bad that 
I had to leave her by herself.

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:12.030
Oh, you're such a sinner, Meroko...

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:13.460
And to think you're a Shinigami...

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.240
Komaki Fuyuko is hard to deal with.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.360
I was so tense the whole time, Takeda-san.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:24.540
I never even knew you could think that way.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.300
Please stop making fun of me.{edited}

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:27.860
Hey Meroko!

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:30.080
Those guys... weren't they reporters from "Monthly SuperStar"?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.090
The ones who just passed by?

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.970
Don't be so weak, Nou-kun.

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:40.450
That Komaki-san must have a good side, too.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:42.980
But there are so many rumors spreading.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.940
That she's hard to deal with... and that she picks on the newcomers...{}

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.900
I heard those too. I'd hate to say
 that those were true.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.700
She probably does those things 
because she cares.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:58.080
To show that she's there to help them...

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:02.660
She was forced to be an idol, or so I heard.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:03.340
Yeah.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:07.510
She didn't like her debut song, 
but she had to sing it.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:11.010
She was depressed and 
began to smoke and drink.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:13.570
As a result, she ruined her voice.

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.120
Her attitude that we see now...

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.770
...is probably the result of that.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.370
I see.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.190
Even so, did she really have a good voice?

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:24.310
Yeah...

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:25.200
Of course.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.010
Somehow, she could light up people's hearts.{Timing}

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:32.990
Nowadays, you can't find 
singers like that anymore.

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:35.000
Really?

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:37.030
So that's how it was...

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:39.850
That's why she got angry that time.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.230
She might be a good person after all.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.500
Let's see...

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:49.180
They took a break and 
said that Sensei's turn is next.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:53.520
Well, I said that we can't do that, but the director insisted.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:54.550
I understand.

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:55.890
R-Really?

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.850
Well, thank you very much.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:00.960
Honestly, what was that novice thinking?

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.390
She was rude to you, Sensei.

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:05.750
This time, she messed up the schedule.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:09.520
She's a really rude person, isn't she, Sensei?

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:12.990
Sensei!{}

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.110
That's what we heard.

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:17.120
I see.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:18.920
So that's why.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.410
I must have sounded so rude
 to Komaki-san earlier.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.540
Well, I have to apologize to her properly.

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:26.520
Yes, you do.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:29.080
Komaki-san's entering.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:32.680
I'm going.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.660
I'm really sorry, Komaki-san.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.890
Alright, alright, stop playing around.

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.590
You should go outside.

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:45.910
But, I...

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:49.440
What's this about?

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:51.230
Eh? What's the meaning of this?

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:53.640
It's time for Sensei's recording.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.690
If you do anything bad, it may throw off Sensei's performance.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.410
Why did that guy throw Mitsuki out?

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:09.020
I'm sure it's because Komaki said so.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:11.790
Just like I thought, she is a mean old hag!

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:14.260
She's really a troublesome novice, isn't she?

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.000
Oh yeah...

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:18.470
Let's take out <i>Full Moon's</i>  performance. {Screw you, hage}

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:21.560
Just put Sensei's new single instead.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.430
S-Sure.

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.530
Wait a sec! What is he saying?

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:26.760
Takuto, we have to tell her.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:27.190
Okay!

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.980
Eh? They're not letting me sing?

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:31.160
Seems like it.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.480
I knew it! She's definitely evil!

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:37.450
That's so... cruel.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:40.860
What's the meaning of this?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.410
Why are you canceling 
<i>Full Moon's</i>  performance?

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:45.990
Can't help it.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:48.810
She was so troublesome to Sensei.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:51.000
That's why we're changing our schedule.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:54.070
Sensei doesn't have free time like you do.

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:56.760
Hey!

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:59.320
Even so, that is too cruel.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:00.110
Mitsuki?

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.230
Komaki-san?

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:12.020
Komaki-san, they said that they won't let me sing... is that true?

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.020
What are you talking about?

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:16.360
Eh? But Tadokoro-san said that...

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.970
I know I've been in your way 
many times, Komaki-san.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.300
But not letting me sing is just too much!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.870
It's my first time on TV.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:28.160
I want to sing... quickly.

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:29.520
Quickly what?

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:32.880
To quickly become a big star that everyone idolizes about?{Edited}

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.340
That's not true.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.650
Well, what is it?

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.800
If that's not true, why else do you want to become a singer?

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.160
I promised...

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.510
I made a promise...

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:44.860
...to someone very dear to me. {Taisetsu=Important/Special, but this flows better imo}

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:47.640
Someone very dear to you?

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:48.840
Yes.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:51.970
I don't know where he is now.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.600
But we made a promise...

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:56.550
...that we'd both work hard 
to achieve our dreams.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:59.110
So, please, let me sing.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.280
You're too naive. {naïve}

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.840
That's just a dream.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:08.300
Once you get into it, 
the promise will be forgotten.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.710
You will sing and sing because it is your job.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:11.330
No, I won't!

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:12.850
Then...

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:21.010
Then Komaki-san is singing
 because it's her job?

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:22.660
Of course.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.720
That's what makes me a pro.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.360
I don't think that way.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:29.640
I don't think that way!

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:34.810
I want to sing with that 
precious feeling inside me.

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.610
If I can't do that, then I'm fine 
with not being a pro.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:42.570
All I want is to touch people's 
hearts with my songs!

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.300
Well, <i>Full Moon</i>-san, please.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:02.510
Eh? But they said I wouldn't sing...

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.340
It's alright.

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:07.260
The idea was from this rotten bald guy.

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:09.380
So, you don't have to worry.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.720
You can sing.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:11.990
Okay!

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:17.000
We'll take it from the top!

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:19.350
Five seconds...

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:20.140
Four.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:21.230
Three.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.990
She's wonderful.

00:19:50.990 --> 00:19:53.990
She's just like a young Komaki Fuyuko.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:04.230
Sensei?{So deserving. How about one on his right too?}

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:07.440
Why did you do such a thing?

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:09.740
Don't even bother to come 
to work from tomorrow.{}

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:11.390
Sensei...

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:14.240
Sensei...!

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:19.390
Hey, look at this!

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:20.980
Ah, Komaki-san!

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:22.400
Eh, Takeda-san too?

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:27.320
You've been involved with new idols lately.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.080
How are they?

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.360
The latest idol, in particular...

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.570
Let's see.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.850
Today, the girl didn't greet me properly.

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:35.520
She looked at my kimono and said that it was like in a Shichigosan.{}

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:39.890
She even had enough energy 
to mess up my schedule.{}

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:42.740
I couldn't even imagine that one person could mess up that badly.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.800
That sounds so troublesome.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:47.520
But...

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:51.360
She was different from all the newcomers I've come across.{}

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:54.800
She even dared to voice her opinions to me.

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:55.970
Oh...

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:58.410
I'm ashamed to admit it, but...

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:04.520
...that girl reminded me of what's important when you become a singer.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:08.680
Once again, I want to go back 
to my original intentions.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.200
Well, Komaki-san, she seems to have left a deep impression on you.

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:13.420
Yes.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.520
It's possible she made me realize my situation.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:24.000
So, until we meet again, 
do your best, Miss Newcomer.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:27.370
I will!

00:23:05.810 --> 00:23:06.940
Takuto, there's trouble!

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:09.810
The paparazzi are onto her!

00:23:09.810 --> 00:23:12.270
At this rate, her secret will...

00:23:12.270 --> 00:23:13.700
Damn it!

00:23:13.980 --> 00:23:16.360
We can't let her secret get out!

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:17.820
Wait for me, Mitsuki!

00:23:17.820 --> 00:23:18.780
I'm coming to help you!

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:19.820
Wait!

00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:22.100
You can't do it alone!

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:22.780
Shut up!

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:24.360
I will...

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:26.750
I will always protect her!

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:29.450
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:30.770
Dangerous Lens
